cs35l56: suspend runtime PM before the first attach

Backport of mainline fbf2c660bac8 ("ASoC: cs35l56: Fix pm_runtime
imbalance if suspending before first attach") to 7.2, where the
interrupt helper is still named cs35l56_disable_sdw_interrupts().

A system suspend before an amplifier has finished its first attach
returned early and skipped pm_runtime_force_suspend(), but resume
always calls pm_runtime_force_resume(), so the runtime PM count went
out of balance. Suspend now always runs, masking the SoundWire
interrupts only while the amplifier is attached.

diff -ruN a/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l56-sdw.c b/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l56-sdw.c
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l56-sdw.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l56-sdw.c
@@ -415,10 +415,8 @@
 {
 	struct cs35l56_private *cs35l56 = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 
-	if (!cs35l56->base.init_done)
-		return 0;
-
-	cs35l56_disable_sdw_interrupts(cs35l56);
+	if (cs35l56->sdw_attached)
+		cs35l56_disable_sdw_interrupts(cs35l56);
 
 	return cs35l56_system_suspend(dev);
 }
